WEBVTT

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.440
Project Mew, an operation to search for Mew,
is underway.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:13.990
Go, who hopes to join the search,
must clear various Pokémon-related Trial Missions.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.000
Every successfully cleared mission
nets the participant a token.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.290
The three candidates who obtain
the most tokens will be accepted.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:30.470
Will Go be able to join the official Mew search team,
and become a Chaser?

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.430
Go!

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.810
Heard you got
your next Trial Mission!

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:36.810
Yeah...

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.560
Someone’s bummed!

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.400
What’s wrong?!

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.320
Well... This time they’re measuring
our battling skills and cooperation.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.280
Battling? That’s great!

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.950
The problem is the cooperation...

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:52.530
Huh?

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.080
It’s a Raid Battle...

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.660
The mission this time...

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.740
What’re you up against?

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.830
The Legendary Pokémon, Freezer...

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:01.790
Whoa! That’s so exciting!

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.340
You getting excited doesn’t help me.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:08.550
But you’ve been in a Raid Battle before,
against that Golugh.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.590
Well... I guess.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.140
Right? With me helping you,
it’ll be fine!

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.560
I’m starting to feel like
I can do it.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.930
Freezer! Freezing Pokémon!
Ice/Flying type!

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.850
A legendary bird Pokémon
that can control ice!

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:26.070
It is said to live in snowy mountains
riddled with permafrost!

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.940
Snowy mountains
riddled with permafrost, huh?

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.070
Where should I look...?

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.200
How about Twins Island?

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.870
Twins Island?

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:37.120
Kikuna,
put it on the main monitor.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:37.870
Right.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:44.710
Twins Island is an island in southern Kanto
with a pair of adjacent mountains.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:50.720
There’s apparently a permafrost cave inside the island
connecting the two mountains.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.390
It wouldn’t be strange
to find Freezer living there.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.350
Thank you, Director.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.430
The future lies in my hands!

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:00.560
Okay then, off to Twins Island...

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:03.690
Let’s go!

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:49.460
Seeking to attempt the Trial Mission,
“Have a Raid Battle against Freezer,”

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.460
Go and Satoshi
have arrived at Twins Island.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:56.090
Will Go be able to
complete the mission?

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.850
A cliff!

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:10.100
That looks like somewhere
we can cross.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.650
Be careful, there’s a strong wind.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.240
Yeah, I know.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:23.910
Golbat?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.630
Pikachu, use 100,000–

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:32.540
I’ve got this!

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.300
Monster Ball, go!

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.050
Nice!

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.480
Golbat’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.140
All right!

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.360
Which way?

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.860
Hmm... I don’t know.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.110
Why don’t we try this way first?

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:57.610
Right.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.410
Another split...

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:04.370
This place is like a maze!

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.200
What do we do?

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.830
Let’s try the left first.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.080
Huh?

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.250
In that case...

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.430
Another dead end?

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.980
One more try!

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.320
This has to be it!

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.740
What’s wrong?

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.410
Are you okay?

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.950
I’ve been lost for ages...

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.040
You’re in Project Mew, too?

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.750
Yeah, I’m a Challenger.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.000
You can come with me, then!

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.380
I’m a Challenger, too!

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:56.590
No...

00:05:56.590 --> 00:06:00.420
My Pokémon are all weakened
from battling Ishitsubute.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:03.260
I can’t have a Raid Battle
with Freezer like this.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.970
You’re giving up?

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.600
I have no choice.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.410
Another split...

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.490
Again?!

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:36.290
Oh, that sounds nice.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:37.500
Yeah.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.090
Wait, a sound...

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:40.420
Then what about...?

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.880
Inteleon, go!

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:47.010
Okay, Sarunori, hit it again!

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:56.270
Inteleon! Pick up the vibrations
in the air and find us the exit!

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.160
In here?

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:16.830
That looks deep...

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.170
Maybe that’s the entrance
to the cave.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:20.840
Thanks, Inteleon.

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:26.550
You should get in
your Ball now too, Sarunori.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:33.890
Freezer will be somewhere
in this cave...

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.940
What is it?

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:43.900
A Gorone!

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:49.950
Monster Ball, go!

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:52.030
Great!

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:00.750
Gorone’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.130
Is that your second catch?!

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:05.050
Yeah, I’m on a roll!

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.760
At this rate,
even Freezer’s no match for me!

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.550
What’s wrong?

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.260
Go, look at this...

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:14.390
A hole?

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.560
Let’s try going down there.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.140
Caterpie, come on!

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.400
String Shot!

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:30.200
Bayleaf! Vine Whip!

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:33.580
Tokio?!

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:35.830
Go!

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:37.710
Huh? Someone you know?

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:40.460
It’s been a while!

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:43.630
So your Chicorita evolved
into Bayleaf?

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:44.550
Yeah!

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:46.800
My Rabbifoot evolved, too!

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.350
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:01.400
All right!

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.310
Now’s your chance
to catch it, Go!

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.820
Then I won’t hold back!

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:07.610
Excellent!!

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:14.780
Pearshen’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.620
Got it!
That’s my third catch today!

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.290
Thanks, Tokio!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.250
You helped me out, too, Go.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:24.920
I nearly ended up dropping out
before even getting to meet Freezer.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:25.750
Huh?

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:29.130
Does that mean you’re
a Project Mew Challenger too?

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.970
Yeah. You are too, right?

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:32.260
Course, yeah.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:33.640
I knew it!

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:36.390
But weren’t you chasing
after Celebi?

00:09:36.390 --> 00:09:37.640
Huh? Celebi?

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.640
Let me introduce you.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:42.690
This is a friend of mine,
and a fellow research fellow.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:45.150
I’m Satoshi. This is Pikachu.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:50.780
I’m Tokio. I became friends with Go long ago
when our paths crossed at a place he was visiting.

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:52.200
This is Bayleaf.

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:54.820
Nice to meet you.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:55.910
Likewise.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:02.620
If you’re chasing after Celebi,
why’re you in Project Mew?

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:03.500
Ah, well...

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:05.920
Celebi’s an Psychic/Grass type.

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.460
I thought that if I track down
every Psychic type, including Mew,

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:12.050
that might lead me
to Celebi, someday.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:14.970
Ooh, you kinda sound like Go.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:18.430
Let’s work hard
and become Chasers!

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:19.600
Yeah!

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:22.640
But first, we need to find Freezer!

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:23.940
That’s right.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:28.820
I met some Challengers
on the way here,

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:32.650
but they all got lost in the maze,
or were attacked by Pokémon...

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.320
We saw them, too.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.070
Can’t we do something for them...?

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:40.040
What do you mean?

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:41.410
I feel sorry for them.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:46.210
They made it all this way to Twins Island...
They were so close to reaching Freezer.

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:49.840
Even so, this is our mission...

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:51.090
Still...

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:53.420
You’re really kind, Tokio.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:56.090
I didn’t mean it like that...

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:58.100
What’s that sound?

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.350
A waterfall!

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:03.430
Let’s have a look!

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.480
What is this thing...?

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.190
I can’t see the basin...

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:21.740
What’s that?

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.370
An ice temple?

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.870
Guess it kinda looks like one.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.830
There’s light shining in
from outside?

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.630
Good grief...

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:33.630
I never expected to see
you two here.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.760
Shigeru?!

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:51.270
What’s that “Good grief...” for?!

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.940
See? It takes <i>nothing</i>
to rile you up.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:55.740
That’s what exasperates me.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.860
Do you know him?

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:01.450
Yeah... He’s not a bad guy,
at least...

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.330
Shigeru.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.330
I’m Tokio.
Nice to meet you.

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.670
We should work together
from here.

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:10.380
Tokio! Don’t just decide that!

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.920
He even waited here
for us, though.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:16.010
Just ‘cause one person
isn’t enough for a Raid Battle!

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:17.260
Correct.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:22.760
The way I see it, clearing the mission
<i>should</i> be priority number one.

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:28.310
I suspect that Freezer
is over there.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.900
So choose.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.770
Will you come investigate
with me or not?

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:34.860
Go...

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:35.860
Let’s go.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:39.150
You’re not scared, are you?

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:40.860
Of course not!

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.530
I’m coming! Just you watch!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:50.620
It’s cold...

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:53.920
Get back!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:04.810
<i>Freezer!</i>

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:07.020
This is a message
from Project Mew.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:10.520
You may use up to three Pokémon
for the Raid Battle.

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:12.150
Recording will begin now.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.740
Here we go!
Everyone, get ready!

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:23.870
You don’t have to tell me!

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.160
Go, Banguirus!

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.950
Hihidaruma, come on!

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:30.620
Negigaknight, I choose you!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.040
You’re up, Yessan!

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:45.350
Stay focused.
Next Pokémon!

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:46.680
Blacky!

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.520
Aceburn, go!

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:49.810
Lucario!

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:51.230
Sirknight!

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:53.020
Eerie Light!

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.200
Absolute Zero?!

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:05.870
A one-hit KO move...

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.740
It’ll sweep you up
if you stick too close!

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.290
Try to battle from a distance!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.380
The Eerie Light confused it.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:20.010
Now’s our chance to attack!

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:21.260
Pyro Ball!

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.260
Aura Sphere!

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.810
The confusion wore off!
Here it comes!

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:39.530
Reflector!

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:40.980
Good choice!

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:46.530
Thanks, Tokio!

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:50.040
Don’t look away!
Focus on the battle!

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:50.910
Windie!

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:53.580
Pyro Ball!

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:54.620
Aura Sphere!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:55.500
Moonforce!

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:03.090
Reflector!

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.690
What was that attack?!

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.270
That’s Triple Axel.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.940
The Reflector
cut its strength in half.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.690
Aceburn and Lucario,
grab onto Freezer!

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:25.450
Don’t just order them around!

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:26.990
Go, let’s do it.

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:32.490
Aceburn, grab onto Freezer!

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.000
You too, Lucario!

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.470
Flamethrower!

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:48.930
Blaze Kick!

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.640
Go, Lucario!

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.690
Heal Pulse!

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.030
Thank you, Tokio.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:11.410
Don’t let your guard down!

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:13.290
Yeah, I know!

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.830
Satoshi,
let’s pile on the pressure!

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:16.710
Yeah!

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:19.750
No! Freezer’s not some
easy little pushover!

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:22.340
Aceburn!
Use Blaze Kick again!

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:24.090
Lucario, use Aura Sphere!

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:29.380
Sirknight, use Light Screen!

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:39.310
Windie! Flamethrower!

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:45.570
Aceburn!

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:49.200
Gantle, come on!

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:50.740
Here we go, Bayleaf!

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:52.820
Pikachu, I choose you!

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:59.040
Go. We’re not alone here.

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:00.290
Let’s work as a team.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:01.830
I know that already!

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:03.340
You don’t understand!

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:05.840
That’s what Shigeru’s
been trying to do!

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:10.470
In a Raid Battle,
you need to cooperate as a team.

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:13.600
It’s such a basic idea,
I never thought to bring it up.

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:18.850
From now on,
you should follow my commands.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:21.810
Have Bayleaf hold Freezer
with Vine Whip.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.610
Then Pikachu, Gantle,
and Windie can attack!

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:28.990
Bayleaf! Vine Whip!

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.450
All right! 100,000 Volts!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:38.580
Flamethrower!

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:45.920
Stone Edge!

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:54.180
It might use Absolute Zero!

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:55.050
Split up!

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.560
No, don’t! If it uses Blizzard,
we’ll all be done for!

00:17:57.560 --> 00:17:59.270
Cluster together behind Gantle!

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.320
Absolute Zero?!

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:10.570
Windie!

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:20.160
Pikachu!

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:27.420
Tokio! Bayleaf can’t
fight Freezer on its own!

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:29.090
No, I have to try.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.340
Bayleaf, use Energy Ball!

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:39.220
Bayleaf!

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.650
The Raid Battle against Freezer
has concluded.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:56.570
Stand by for contact from HQ.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:19:01.290
Freezer was really strong...

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:03.960
Go?

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:09.210
Tokio... If you guys weren’t here...
I wouldn’t have stood a chance.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.960
Don’t say that.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:16.300
You taking the front line allowed me
to focus on defense and recovery moves.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:20.310
You’re too optimistic.

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:25.390
The Raid Battle would’ve gone better
if not for his selfish actions.

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:30.070
Mr. Tsurugi.

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:33.360
We’ve collected valuable data
on Freezer.

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:34.650
Thank you.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:38.530
As proof of clearing the mission,
we will send you each three tokens.

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:41.280
Furthermore...

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:47.210
Shigeru gets one extra token for his strong leadership,
and Tokio for his dedication to teamwork.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:54.590
Mr. Tsurugi. Is cooperation
going to be necessary for finding Mew?

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.390
Think about that yourself.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:02.470
Let me say something, too.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:06.560
A certain <i>someone</i> used to be selfish,
and a poor team player,

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:09.520
and he still managed to get picked
to be a Chaser somehow.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:12.110
That will be all.

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:15.530
Well, this is where
I say goodbye.

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:16.360
Right...

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.610
Cheer up, Go.

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:20.740
There’ll be more missions.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.870
If you keep at it,
I’m sure you’ll make it!

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:24.120
Thanks.

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:27.120
Sometimes,
kindness can be a cruelty.

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:31.250
Accepting someone who isn’t ready,
allowing them hopes and dreams,

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:34.880
and forcing them beyond their means
can lead to the worst possible outcome.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:36.880
What do you mean by that?

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:41.640
I cooperated with you today
because the mission was a Raid Battle,

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:45.220
but we Challengers don’t need to
play nice and pretend to be friends.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:50.560
It’s fine! We can help
each other out as friends!

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.900
You’re as naïve as ever.

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:56.820
I agree with Mr. Tsurugi’s
strict mentality.

00:20:56.820 --> 00:21:00.450
Without that strictness,
we’ll never encounter Mew.

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:09.410
You’re starting to realize that now,
aren’t you, Go?

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:12.920
First time you’ve said my name
in a friendly tone.

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:18.630
By provoking people,
you make them realize something new.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:21.800
I’m starting to understand
your ways too, Shigeru.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:24.930
And that’s the first time
you’ve even <i>said</i> my name.

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:27.350
I look forward to our next meeting.

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:28.520
See you!

00:21:31.230 --> 00:21:35.690
Go, Tokio, and Shigeru have
cleared the mission with flying colors.

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:40.900
Will the three of them be chosen
as Project Mew members?

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.620
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:15.870
My opponent this time is Ms. Drasna
of the Kalos Elite Four!

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:19.290
And she’s a Dragon user.

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:20.960
She’ll be a tough opponent!

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:22.800
I thought this might happen...

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:25.510
The time has come for science
to usher in our future!

00:23:25.510 --> 00:23:27.430
Citronic Gear, on!

00:23:27.430 --> 00:23:29.640
I’m Eureka.
Nice to meet you!

00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:31.430
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:34.230
Satoshi and Citron!
The Great Friendship Training!!
